README for RudeConfig
See the end of file for copying conditions


*** INTRODUCTION ***

RudeConfig is a library that allows applications to (painlessly) read,
modify, and create config / .ini files.

Full documentation, including a quick start and API notes, is in README.md.


*** BUILDING ***

RudeConfig builds with CMake:

	cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
	cmake --build build
	ctest --test-dir build
	cmake --install build

Then include <rude/config.h> and link with -lrudeconfig, or use
find_package(rudeconfig) from CMake, or pkg-config.

The supported build system is CMake. The earlier autotools build is available
in the v6.0.1 tag for projects that still rely on that workflow; CMake is the
recommended option for current ARM and x86 platforms.

